### Analysis Summary
None of the target libraries serve as functional replacements for Javassist. They address fundamentally different problem domains:
- Most are application frameworks (HiveMind, RESTEasy providers)
- Several are utilities (Commons Lang, JEXL)
- Others are specialized tools (Ehcache, JGroups, XStream)
- NLP libraries are completely unrelated domains

Javassist's core competency - runtime bytecode manipulation for AOP and dynamic code generation - remains unique among these candidates. Modern alternatives like Byte Buddy (not in this list) would be better replacements as they solve the same core problem with more modern APIs./n
